#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0283 expect=noViolation domain=SE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the SEENDTC of the subject's last Subject Element (highest SESEQ) is after the subject disposition date (DS.DSSTDTC); the last Element must end on or before the disposition date.
#note "POLARITY PIN, silent direction -- the partner of CDISC-SEND-0283-invalid-SE-1.cdt and the case that proves the pre-Fix-#158 rule was inverted rather than merely mis-scoped. The last Subject Element (SESEQ=2) ends 2020-01-15, EXACTLY the disposition date DS.DSSTDTC=2020-01-15. The Source Rule -- 'The value of SEENDTC for the last Element must immediately precede or be the same as the value of DS.DSSTDTC for the subject' -- names equality as CONFORMANT in terms, so the rule must be silent here. Under the authored date_less_than_or_equal_to it was not: the comparison was true, every conjunct held, and the rule REPORTED this conforming subject. That is the measured over-report this fixture pins shut; it is RED against the pre-fix rule. NOT vacuous for want of data: is_last_in_group resolves (row 2 is the last element), the DS join key USUBJID matches, and DSSTDTC is populated -- changing 2020-01-15 to 2020-01-16 on the SE row makes this same file fire, which is the invalid sibling."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-10
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | TRT | 2020-01-10 | 2020-01-15
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-15
---
